    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0694" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.631</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-05T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                                1918, 1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 140, December 31, 6 p.m. In case of necessity you may draw not exceeding
                    $5,000 for sending indigent Americans out of the country. If imperative to leave
                    Moscow you should go to some place other than Rostov or headquarters of any
                    sectional movement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
